    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89317" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσεταιρ-ίζομαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		 with pf.
		
			Pass.
		, also plpf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσηταίριστο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					58.4
				</span></i>
			:—<i>take to oneself as a friend, associate with
				oneself</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cat.Mi.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ κατά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pisc.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			; in bad sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐς
			πανδοχεῖον</span> Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Philopatr.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; <i>take into partnership, secure the approval of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δῆμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.66
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πλήθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					2.40
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>associate oneself with</i> another, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ax.</u>
				369b
			</span></i>.</div>
